# Stray build artifacts: stale build/<pkg> dirs left over from packages that
# used to be ament_python (setup.py + <pkg>/<pkg>/ module layout) can make
# CMake's linker write a compiled executable straight into the source tree
# at <pkg>/<pkg> once the package is re-pointed at CMakeLists.txt/ament_cmake
# (see face_detection/face_detection, added by mistake in 6c978d7). Ignore
# that exact self-named path per already-ported package so a `git add -A`
# can't recommit one.
/face_detection/face_detection
/person_detection/person_detection
/animate_behavior/animate_behavior
/gesture_execution/gesture_execution
/overt_attention/overt_attention

# VS Code workspace state. browse.vc.db is the C++ IntelliSense index and
# reaches ~1.2 GB per package -- it was the single largest thing in this
# workspace before being deleted twice.
.vscode/

# CycloneDDS drops this wherever a node is launched from
cyclonedds.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consolidated from the per-package .gitignore files that used to live in
# pepper_navigation/, pepper_navigation/map/ and pepper_navigation/pcd/.
# One file at the repo root is easier to audit than four scattered ones; the
# reasoning each of them carried is kept below rather than dropped.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# colcon scratch. NOT anchored with a leading slash on purpose: colcon drops
# these wherever it is run, and a build started from e.g.
# pepper_navigation/rviz/ put build/, install/ and log/ THERE. Anchored rules
# matched only the package root, so those nested copies were
# untracked-but-not-ignored and got committed by a `git add -A` (268ced6).
# Matching at any depth stops that.
#
# Now repo-wide rather than pepper_navigation-only: the reason above is a
# property of colcon, not of that one package, and pepper_slam/build/ was
# equally committable before this.
build/
install/
log/

# Editor/tool backups, also repo-wide for the same reason. nav2_config writes
# <file>.yaml.bak before each save (one level only -- each save overwrites it),
# and utils/align_map.py writes .bak beside the map artifacts it rotates.
# Neither belongs in the repo, and without this a `git add -A` sweeps them in.
*.bak

# The 3D prior maps are binary that changes wholesale on every mapping run, so
# they are deliberately NOT tracked -- copy them to a new machine instead:
#   scp <file>.pcd <host>:~/ros2_ws/src/pepper4dec/pepper_navigation/<dir>/
# then colcon build, which installs them into the package share where the
# launch defaults look. The 2D grids, *_poses.txt and the ScanContext
# pose .json ARE tracked: they are small and they identify the map.
#
# The ** matters: pcd/ holds sc_pcd_<run>/ subdirectories of per-keyframe
# clouds (2735 files, 75 MB for the current run), and a plain
# /pepper_navigation/pcd/*.pcd would match only the top level and let those
# through. Scoped to these two directories rather than repo-wide so a small
# .pcd committed deliberately elsewhere is not silently swallowed.
/pepper_navigation/map/**/*.pcd
/pepper_navigation/pcd/**/*.pcd

# pytest writes .pytest_cache/ with its own self-ignoring .gitignore inside.
# Those inner files are regenerated on every run, so they are left alone;
# this makes the whole directory ignored regardless of whether pytest's own
# file is present.
.pytest_cache/
